#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:5
#: 8faecfe51c7c43429dfcca2b01f226ff
msgid "QuadPlane VTOL Tuning Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:7
#: 5589c893b61d403da906eae6f39eb4de
msgid "This section provides an overview of how to tune various QuadPlane VTOL parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:9
#: ed14ded6fb7f453b95f9eea27c0caf1f
msgid "For normal Quadplanes follow :ref:`quadplane-vtol-tuning-process` for detailed tuning steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:10
#: c9a7b2993cbe49459fbd5254a1b38e4b
msgid "For Tailsitters, see :ref:`tailsitter-tuning-guide`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:11
#: 5d4fda2eb0244b07aec37b38333d8ece
msgid "For non-tailsitter Quadplanes with tilt rotors for vectored YAW, see :ref:`tilt-vectored-yaw-tuning` in addition to :ref:`quadplane-vtol-tuning-process`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:14
#: 409f5fbf44bb4192b9ddb79a0faea463
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:16
#: 291b1dba52a542d38f0405afe752526c
msgid "The default parameters controlling the VTOL motors PID loops should allow most frames to initially hover controllably, if the motors' mechanics are setup and aligned correctly and escs calibrated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:18
#: 67678119e3844eba9f76fe742f2476d8
msgid "The most important parameters controlling stability are the Roll/Pitch/Yaw PIDS. For altitude control, the vertical position controller's parameters and Motor Thrust Scaling parameters, and for navigation/loiter the Loiter controllers's parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:20
#: a210372e98e045c08bebc09f269f6ce1
msgid "Normally, it's best to start by tuning the Rate Roll/Pitch P in QSTABILIZE mode then move onto tuning altitude hold in QHOVER mode, then QLOITER (which often needs no tuning) and finally the waypoint navigation performance in Auto mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:25
#: c6dd688b03964c73896818eac02a2d41
msgid "for Tailsitter QuadPlanes, some axes need a slightly different PID tuning approach depending on the exact frame configuration used. Be sure to also read :ref:`TailSitter Tuning <tailsitter-tuning-guide>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:28
#: d211e3cebe4a44f5a6789e97b662d055
msgid "Filter tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:30
#: f0ba332e6e6247e39c749f55aa95b0a3
msgid "QuadPlanes are often affected by vibration and tuning the various software filters available is critical to achieving an optimum overall tune. A guide on tuning the various notch filters available can be found on the :ref:`Notch Filtering wiki page <common-imu-notch-filtering>`. A optimum tune will be obtained on the D terms, below, if the filtering has been optimized first. However, in many circumstances reasonable performance can be obtained with just PID tuning the P terms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:34
#: 693cfb4f8744489898ceded5f10c5bc8
msgid "Roll/Pitch tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:36
#: 4392142276404d38bd309bb88b401e5c
msgid "The ``Q_A_RAT_RLL_x`` and ``Q_A_RAT_PIT_x`` Roll/Pitch Rate parameters which convert the desired rotation rate into a motor output are the most important. If not a tailsitter, then the ``Q_A_RAT_PIT_FF`` will be zero and corrections are dominated by P/I/D. In tailsitters, then the FF terms dominate (Pitch axis only) and P/D are primarily for disturbance correction. For tuning tailsitter pitch axis, see :ref:`pitch-yaw-tuning`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:38
#: 2714b1012f7c42f1a542cae72a2572c0
msgid "The :ref:`Q_A_ANG_RLL_P<Q_A_ANG_RLL_P>` and :ref:`Q_A_ANG_PIT_P<Q_A_ANG_PIT_P>` Roll/Pitch P converts the desired angle into a desired rotation rate which is then fed to the Rate controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:40
#: 4033e219db2449598b61296d7508099d
msgid "A higher value will make the QuadPlane more responsive to roll/pitch inputs, a lower value will make it smoother"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:42
#: b62361bd882b4b66a461720296f2c675
msgid "If set too high, the QuadPlane will oscillate on the roll and/or pitch axis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:44
#: 9ebae13dc085468ab59b1d89f49e5f43
msgid "If set too low the QuadPlane will become sluggish to inputs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:46
#: e664744c0d3e4588817f2b143acb46b0
msgid "An objective view of the overall Roll and Pitch performance can be seen by graphing the :ref:`dataflash log's <common-downloading-and-analyzing-data-logs-in-mission-planner>` ATT message's DesRoll vs Roll and DesPit vs Pitch. The \"Roll\" (i.e. actual roll) should closely follow the \"DesRoll\" while in stabilized modes. Pitch should similarly closely follow DesPit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:50
#: 79b5cf3ac32541e581399ac50bcb53b4
msgid "Alternatively you may wish to try automatically tuning the rate parameters using the :ref:`QUICKTUNE <quicktune>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:53
#: 1a27890740e949e2a64b48ca1deaca1d
msgid "Yaw Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:55
#: 08ffe877b719470db8fbafc26d51e8fa
msgid "The Angle Yaw and Rate Yaw parameters control the yaw response. With QuadPlanes, these often need tuning to get the desired YAW response, since configurations vary widely. In non-tailsitters, then the ``Q_A_RAT_YAW_FF`` will be zero and corrections are dominated by P/I/D. But in tailsitters, the FF term dominates and P/D are primarily for disturbance correction. For tuning a tailsitter yaw axis, see :ref:`pitch-yaw-tuning`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:57
#: 32e602df01f1425e94aceae9bb78ac8b
msgid "Similar to roll and pitch, if either :ref:`Q_A_RAT_YAW_P<Q_A_RAT_YAW_P>` or :ref:`Q_A_ANG_YAW_P<Q_A_ANG_YAW_P>` is too high the QuadPlane's heading will oscillate. If they are too low, the QuadPlane may be unable to maintain its heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:59
#: cfe3b197446c44d5aeac21b179f0c363
msgid "The :ref:`Q_A_ANG_YAW_P<Q_A_ANG_YAW_P>` is the gain on the error between the autopilots desired heading and actual heading which is fed into the Rate controller to demand a rotation rate. The :ref:`Q_A_RAT_YAW_P<Q_A_RAT_YAW_P>` is the gain applied to the difference between demanded rotation rate and actual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:61
#: 52b880f0ac3545a19ce0685b399e4f6f
msgid "The :ref:`Q_YAW_RATE_MAX<Q_YAW_RATE_MAX>` parameter controls how quickly QuadPlane rotates based on a pilot’s yaw input in stabilized modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:64
#: 9547d5af7e1b41a497d6f87e1b70c793
msgid "Altitude Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:66
#: 00db20335ce14cbcac2938ec84de5c1a
msgid "The QHOVER (altitude hold) related tuning parameters are related to the vertical position controller and the motor thrust scaling, which linearizes the throttle to motor thrust response to improve the position controllers response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:68
#: 3066a1d802184ec0a8a64683a27c1e56
msgid "The ``Q_P_POSZ_P`` parameter is used to convert the altitude error (the difference between the desired altitude and the actual altitude) to a desired climb or descent rate. A higher rate will make it more aggressively attempt to maintain it’s altitude but if set too high leads to a jerky throttle response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:70
#: d38ed1bd81aa421da2bb32dd71ec0c87
msgid "The :ref:`Q_P_D_VEL_P<Q_P_D_VEL_P>` (which normally requires no tuning) converts the desired climb or descent rate into a desired acceleration up or down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:72
#: b60e32ba022b49339833e261141d65d0
msgid "The :ref:`Q_P_D_ACC_P<Q_P_D_ACC_P>`, :ref:`Q_P_D_ACC_I<Q_P_D_ACC_I>`, and :ref:`Q_P_D_ACC_D<Q_P_D_ACC_D>` PID gains convert the acceleration error (i.e the difference between the desired acceleration and the actual acceleration) into a motor output. The 1:2 ratio of P to I (i.e. I is twice the size of P) should be maintained if you modify these parameters. These values should never be increased but for very powerful QuadPlane VTOL motors you may get better response by reducing both by 50% (i.e P to 0.5, I to 1.0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:75
#: 228c3456be974c909599bbd31716752c
msgid "Loiter Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:77
#: afb2e77127514a0a873565a2afabfc2d
msgid "Generally if Roll and Pitch are tuned correctly,  the :ref:`GPS <common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs_gps_glitches>` and :ref:`compass <common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs_compass_interference>` are set-up and performing well and :ref:`vibration levels <common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs_vibrations>` are acceptable, Loiter does not require much tuning but please see the :ref:`Loiter Mode <qloiter-mode>` page for more details on tunable parameters including the horizontal speed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:86
#: f9cc1981c08f428480aea519b33d0d95
msgid "In-flight Tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:88
#: 8cf068d2ee29465a8a4d04d150e922dc
msgid "Many parameters can be tuned while in flight, see :ref:`common-transmitter-tuning`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:92
#: cffb20f01a094608a5c8f304b7325b29
msgid "Video introduction to PIDs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:94
#: 7cdff375a1ce4be2a29e988021f7b69a
msgid "PIDs (Proportional - Integral - Derivative) are the method used by our firmware to continuously stabilize the vehicle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:97
#: c5b4b506f89d4ee69463c326e1264d3f
msgid "Proportional = Immediate Correction: The further off you are the bigger the correction you make."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:99
#: 740ad83c7cc04149a3c3a27846039502
msgid "Integral = Over time or steady state correction: If we are failing to make progress add additional correction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-vtol-tuning.rst:101
#: af0b47741c924eb6ad9956e68c292524
msgid "Derivative = Take it Easy correction: Is the correction going to fast? if it is slow it down (dampen) it a bit to avoid overshoot."
msgstr ""
